From d2be8fce5c4ba6aad361e3889419775d95991bb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "joey.qu" <yal3ay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:08:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] xz1c-engine: pool DoT connections and retry closed idle
 ones

DoT queries shared one connection behind a mutex, so parallel lookups
queued behind each other, and the first query after the server closed
an idle connection failed with EOF.

Keep up to 4 DoT connections, drop idle ones older than 20s, and retry
once on a fresh connection when a reused one fails. Only successful
queries update validation state; failures are left to the validation
thread so a single lost packet no longer reports the server as broken.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I076e5c8adc26d95ae5a101c5f56854e0792161b3
